# Global gitignore — applies to EVERY repo on a device that symlinks this file.
# Linked to ~/.config/git/ignore by setup.sh (git's default user-level ignore path;
# core.excludesfile is deliberately left unset so the default applies).
#
# Lives here, in the synced dotfiles, because an ignore rule that exists on only one
# machine is a coincidence, not a rule — a new device silently starts without it and
# commits the very files this is meant to exclude.

# Claude Code writes per-device permission approvals here. They are machine-specific
# by design (see ~/.claude/rules/claude-config.md), so they must never be committed.
# NOTE: gitignore only affects UNTRACKED files. If one of these is already tracked in
# a repo, this line does nothing there — untrack it first:
#   git rm --cached .claude/settings.local.json
# and add the path to that repo's own .gitignore so the fix survives on every device.
**/.claude/settings.local.json
